A||||9||mrfixit58||Auto Trans Over-Drive?||||5||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||02-24-2000||04:20 PM||||From what I've learned from this forum, I know you can use the 5-speed tranny out of a Beretta but what about the automatic? Didn't some of the Beretta's come with overdrive? Would the Rodney Dickman kit work? IF the transmission would work, does anyone know the first gear ratio?<P>Thanks,<BR>Roy L.||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||02-24-2000||07:16 PM||||I don't think he has a kit for an auto.<P>Automatics aren't that hard to deal with. The shifter brackets don't take the abuse the manual trany cars do.<P>One thing you will need to do is measure the distance from the bell housing/motor line to the ends of the axle openings. if that is diferant then you'll need diferant half shafts. You might need them anyway if the AOD uses diferant inner CV's.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||02-25-2000||07:28 AM||||Thanks Ogre,<P>I'm going to the junk yard today and I'll poke around. How about anyone else? Anyone done a automatic OD swap???<P>Roy L.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||02-25-2000||11:59 AM||||If you use the overdrive automatic from a Grand Prix (which most folks use when they swap in a 3800) you will need to use different axles. (The splines are different.) A.C.E. sells these axles. <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.americancustomeng.com/</A> <BR>Not sure about the Beretta automatic. I think it may be a different (smaller) trans. Sure would be nice if it used the same axles as the 125-C.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||02-25-2000||05:17 PM||||I tried calling my Fiero buddy at the local Chevrolet dealer to see if he could get anything out of his computer regarding compatability but, no luck. <P>I've got a lot of experience with cars of the late sixties and early seventies but not much with any thing that uses a CV joint. And, I'm a little intimidated by them. I guess until I have to, I'll remain a CV virgin.<P>If anyone has a spare axle and gets an oppertunity to compair it with the Beretta OD unit, it would be great info to add to the collective knowledge here at the Forum.<P>Roy L.||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||02-25-2000||05:51 PM||||The problem is that the 440 or 4T60 (don't even think about the 4T60E trans. You can control it without the later ECM) uses larger axles. However, I believe the spines into the trans are the same. It's possible the Fiero axles will fit into the 440.<P>What I would do is head to a Pick-n-Pull, grab and axle from any 125C car and try plugging it into a 440. At the same time, look for a car with a rebuilt 440. They will have a silver GM remanufactured label on the side cover. These should have all of the updates and you could probably pick one up cheap. <P>I've swapped 4T60/E's and 440's, but not into a 125C axle set. But I have heard people talk about them using the 125C axles with a 440/4T60.<P>Another option is to call CV's Unlimited (on the web) at 1-800-868-0057. Tell them you are trying to install a 440 in place of a 125C in a GM. They know all of the axles lengths available and can confirm if the inner CV splines are the same or not. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 02-25-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfixit58||02-25-2000||06:56 PM||||TerryK,<P>That's just the kind of info I was looking for. Unfortunatly, I'll probably habe to wait until Monday to call. Oh well, that will just add to the excitment.<P>What is the significants to the GM remanufactured label on the side cover? was there a recall on the 440? And, if so, did they fix it?<P>Roy L.<P>||||reg||14
Z||000007||terryk||02-25-2000||11:17 PM||||Early 440's had some problems. The label just means it's a factory rebuild 440 with the updates.<P>The 440 is essentially a 125C with overdrive tacked on.<P>You can also measure the width from axle seal to seal on the trans. <P>Lastly, the PN swithes are on the trans of a 440, not on the shifter in the console.<P>Frankly, I'm not sure I would bother with the swap unless a BUICK WAS DRIVING IT! EEEEEHAAAA!<P>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 02-26-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 02-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||DRH||02-28-2000||06:18 PM||||I ran across this link and thought you might be interested.<BR> <A HREF="http://hometown.aol.com/kit440t4/myhomepage/business.html" TARGET=_blank>http://hometown.aol.com/kit440t4/myhomepage/business.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfixit58||02-28-2000||07:13 PM||||Thanks for the heads up. I've bookmarked that page for the future.||||reg||14
